>>When do shops close for inventory?  Just curious.  Thanks.

>As far as I know, it's when you need them most.  Sometimes there's a
>message written in the dust outside the door, and other times there
>isn't (scuffed out by monsters?).

Not exactly, in my experience. There are three kinds of doors: open
ones, closed ones, and locked ones. If there is no message written in
the dust ("closed for inventory"), the door is closed, but not locked.
You can just open it and the shopkeeper won't mind. If the door is
LOCKED, however, there is always the message. If you don't see a
message, you can just open the door (you shouldn't make a habit of
kicking down doors: it's impolite :-).

